# fifine Deck — credentials template
#
#   cp -n .env.template .env   then fill in what you actually use
#
# `-n` because a .env you already have holds live tokens, and a plain cp
# would overwrite them.
#
# Put the .env NEXT TO FifineDeck.app (that is, in this folder). It is found
# from the app's own location, not the working directory — launched from
# Finder that would be `/`. Nothing here is required to use the deck: every
# widget except Stocks and the Spotify *account* source works with the file
# absent, and so does every part of the app except generated artwork.
#
# This file is a template and is committed. `.env` itself is gitignored, and
# must stay that way — it holds live tokens.
#
# Three places are searched for each value, first hit wins:
#   1. the process environment      FINNHUB_KEY=… open FifineDeck.app
#   2. widgets.json                 what the widget editor's Save writes
#   3. this file
# widgets.json deliberately beats .env, so pressing Save always takes effect.
# If a value here looks ignored, that is why — the editor says, per field,
# which source it came from. **Reload** there re-reads this file without a
# relaunch.


# ── Stocks ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A free key from https://finnhub.io — sign up, copy the key from the
# dashboard. Free tier is 60 calls/minute, which is far more than the deck
# uses: one quote cache is shared by every widget and no symbol is refetched
# more than once every 5 seconds.
#
# Without it the Stocks widget draws "no API key" on the key.
FINNHUB_KEY=

# The same value under the spelling an older .env of this project used. Set
# one or the other, not both; FINNHUB_KEY is checked first.
#FINNHUN=


# ── Spotify ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ONLY needed for Source = "your Spotify account", which follows playback on
# any device — your phone, a speaker. The default source, "Spotify on this
# Mac", needs NOTHING here: it asks the desktop app what is playing over
# Apple Events. If the deck only ever plays music from this Mac, stop reading.
#
# Setup, in order:
#
#   1. https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard → Create app. Any name.
#   2. Redirect URI — this exact string, no trailing slash:
#
#          http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
#
#      NOT http://localhost:8888/callback. Spotify matches the redirect
#      literally, and the app's login listener binds 127.0.0.1, so the two
#      spellings are not interchangeable — a mismatch fails with
#      INVALID_CLIENT: Invalid redirect URI before you ever see a login page.
#   3. Tick the **Web API** box.
#   4. Copy the Client ID into SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID below. Leave the client
#      SECRET where it is — the login uses PKCE and never sends one.
#   5. In the widget editor, press **Connect Spotify…**. A browser opens, you
#      approve, and the refresh token is written to widgets.json for you.
#
# Port 8888 has to be free while you do step 5, and only while you do it.
# The scopes requested are user-read-playback-state (to see what is playing)
# and user-modify-playback-state (so a transport key can act).
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=

# Normally you never set this by hand — step 5 obtains it. Paste one here
# only if you already have a token for the same client id, e.g. moving a
# working setup to another Mac.
#
# Note it will not stay here: Spotify rotates refresh tokens, and the app
# saves the rotated one to widgets.json — which then outranks this file.
# Treat this line as a way in, not as the store.
SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=


# ── Generated artwork ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A key from https://fal.ai — Dashboard → Keys. Enables the **Generate** field
# under Artwork in the key editor, and under "Image across deck" in the Deck
# card: type what you want, press Make, and it lands on the hardware in about
# a second.
#
# The model is Ideogram v4 instant (ideogram/v4/instant). Every press is a
# paid API call against your fal balance — small, but not free, so the button
# takes one press at a time rather than queueing.
#
# Pictures are written to
# ~/Library/Application Support/FifineDeck/Generated/ and referenced from
# settings.json by path. Deleting one blanks the key that used it.
#
# Without a key the Generate field is disabled and says so; nothing else is
# affected.
FAL_KEY=


# ── Where this file is found ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# FIFINE_DECK_ENV overrides the search with an explicit path. It is read from
# the ENVIRONMENT, so setting it in here does nothing — the file has to be
# found before it can be read. Export it in your shell instead:
#
#     FIFINE_DECK_ENV=~/secrets/deck.env open FifineDeck.app
